// WebhookEventType CloudEvent type a webhook subscription or notification channel can subscribe to. Legacy internal event names (e.g. 'Resource.Alarm.Create') are still accepted on write and are normalized to the matching CloudEvent type. GET /api/v1/eventTypes, and this schema's 'x-monotaur-event-catalogue' extension, describe each type and the JSON Schema of its payload.
//
// - `com.monotaur.alarm.triggered`: An alarm opened: its monitor went to Fault with no alarm open, or an open alarm was created through the API. Sent once per alarm; withheld while the alarm is squelched.
// - `com.monotaur.alarm.cleared`: An open alarm closed: its monitor recovered or was deleted, or the alarm's end was set through the API. Sent once per alarm.
// - `com.monotaur.alarm.acknowledged`: An open alarm was acknowledged with POST /api/v1/alarms/{id}/acknowledge. Sent once per alarm; acknowledging it again sends nothing. Delivered even while the alarm is squelched.
// - `com.monotaur.alarm.note-added`: A note was added to an alarm's incident timeline with POST /api/v1/alarmNotes. Sent once per note; editing or deleting a note sends nothing. Delivered even while the alarm is squelched.
// - `com.monotaur.monitor.status-changed`: A monitor's status changed value: sample evaluation, a heartbeat, a heartbeat or alert expiration, or a PATCH. Message-only changes send nothing.
// - `com.monotaur.monitor.no-data`: A monitor's probe missed its scheduled runs without delivering a sample and the monitor entered its no-data state. Sent once per entry into the state.
// - `com.monotaur.monitor.heartbeat-missed`: A Heartbeat monitor's heartbeat did not arrive before its status expired, and the monitor was faulted. Sent once per missed heartbeat, with monitor.status-changed.
// - `com.monotaur.monitor.created`: A monitor was created through the API. Restoring a deleted monitor does not send it.
// - `com.monotaur.monitor.deleted`: A monitor was deleted through the API (a soft delete; it can be restored).
// - `com.monotaur.probe.execution-failed`: A sample arrived in which at least one sensor reading is an execution error (status "error", ADR-0032) and the monitor's previous sample had none. Sent once when the probe starts failing, not for every failed run.
// - `com.monotaur.component.status-changed`: A component's aggregated status changed value. Sent once per change.
// - `com.monotaur.maintenance-window.upcoming`: A maintenance window starts within the prestart lead time (MaintenanceWindows:PrestartLeadTime, default 15 minutes). Sent once each time the window enters the lead time.
// - `com.monotaur.maintenance-window.started`: A maintenance window became active.
// - `com.monotaur.maintenance-window.stopped`: A maintenance window that was sent started ended, or was moved so it is no longer active.
// - `com.monotaur.webhook-subscription.auto-disabled`: Webhook delivery disabled a subscription after too many deliveries in a row failed (Webhooks:Delivery:AutoDisableAfterConsecutiveFailures). Sent to the other subscriptions and to notification channels.
// - `com.monotaur.notification-channel.auto-disabled`: Notification delivery disabled a channel after too many deliveries in a row failed (Notifications:Delivery:AutoDisableAfterConsecutiveFailures). Sent to webhook subscriptions and to the other channels.
type WebhookEventType string

